{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.DilogPartAConvergence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DilogPartAConvergence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.DilogReflection","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.DilogPartARiemannSum","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Convex.Slope","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Convex.SpecificFunctions.Basic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.partialProduct_to_LiTwo_Ioo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.partialProduct_to_LiTwo_Ioo","kind":"theorem","line":355,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartAConvergence.lean#L355-L366","doc":"**Unconditional Part-A limit on `(0,1)`.**  With `archimedeanLimit_Ioo` the\n`[ArchimedeanLimit x]` typeclass gate on the conditional consumer\n`partialProduct_to_LiTwo` is discharged for every `x ∈ (0,1)`: the Faddeev-\nscaling convergence `(1-q)·log Φ_n(x;q) → Li₂(x)` holds outright, no instance\nhypothesis required. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.archimedeanLimit_Ioo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.archimedeanLimit_Ioo","kind":"theorem","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartAConvergence.lean#L265-L353","doc":"**B3.5 — Part-A convergence.**  For `0 < x < 1`, the Faddeev-scaling limit\n`(1-q)·log Φ_n(x;q) → Li₂(x)` holds: `ArchimedeanLimit x`.  Assembled from the\nRiemann-sum identity (Bricks 1–2), the telescoping error bound\n(`riemann_error_bound`), the tail bound (`tail_bound`), and the target integral\n(`integral_zero_one_eq_LiTwo`).  This discharges the last open field of Part A\nof `conj:dilogarithm-archimedean-limit`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.pow_le_exp_neg_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.pow_le_exp_neg_mul","kind":"theorem","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartAConvergence.lean#L254-L263","doc":"`qⁿ ≤ exp(−n·(1−q))` for `0 < q` (from `log q ≤ q − 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.tail_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.tail_bound","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartAConvergence.lean#L233-L250","doc":"**B3.4 — tail bound.**  `0 ≤ ∫₀^b h ≤ b·x/(1-x)` for `0 < b ≤ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.h_intervalIntegrable_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.h_intervalIntegrable_zero","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartAConvergence.lean#L211-L231","doc":"Tail integrability: `h` is interval-integrable on `[0,b]` for `0 < b ≤ 1`\n(continuous on `(0,b]`, bounded by `x/(1-x)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.h_bounds_Ioc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.h_bounds_Ioc","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartAConvergence.lean#L189-L209","doc":"`0 ≤ h(u) ≤ x/(1-x)` on `(0,1]` (the integrand is bounded near `0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.riemann_error_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.riemann_error_bound","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartAConvergence.lean#L132-L185","doc":"**B3.3b — the Riemann-sum error bound.**  The left-Riemann sum\n`S_n = Σ_{k<n} h(qᵏ)·(qᵏ − qᵏ⁺¹)` over-estimates `∫_{qⁿ}^1 h` by at most\n`(1-q)·(h(1) − h(qⁿ))`:  `0 ≤ S_n − ∫_{qⁿ}^1 h ≤ (1-q)·(h(1) − h(qⁿ))`.\nProof by induction: each step adds a cell whose error is squeezed by the\nper-cell bounds (B3.3a) and telescopes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.h_integral_ge_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.h_integral_ge_left","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartAConvergence.lean#L116-L128","doc":"**B3.3 lower cell bound.**  `h(a)·(b−a) ≤ ∫_a^b h` on `[a,b] ⊆ (0,1]`\n(monotone: `h(a)` is the min). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.h_integral_le_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.h_integral_le_right","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartAConvergence.lean#L102-L114","doc":"**B3.3 upper cell bound.**  `∫_a^b h ≤ h(b)·(b−a)` on `[a,b] ⊆ (0,1]`\n(monotone: `h(b)` is the max). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.h_intervalIntegrable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.h_intervalIntegrable","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartAConvergence.lean#L94-L100","doc":"`h` is interval-integrable on any `[a,b] ⊆ (0,1]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.h_continuousOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.h_continuousOn","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartAConvergence.lean#L81-L92","doc":"`h(u) = −log(1 - x u)/u` is continuous on any `[a,b] ⊆ (0,1]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.h_monotoneOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.h_monotoneOn","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartAConvergence.lean#L65-L77","doc":"**B3.2 — monotonicity.**  `h(u) = −log(1 - x u)/u` is monotone increasing on\n`(0,1]` for `0 < x < 1`.  Convex-slope: with `g(u) = −log(1 - x u)` convex and\n`g(0) = 0`, `h(u) = (g u − g 0)/(u − 0)` is a secant slope from `0`, which is\nmonotone for a convex function (`ConvexOn.secant_mono`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.convexOn_neg_log_one_sub_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.convexOn_neg_log_one_sub_mul","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartAConvergence.lean#L46-L63","doc":"Convexity of `g(u) = −log(1 - x u)` on `[0,1]` — `log` is concave on `(0,∞)`,\n`u ↦ 1 - x u` is affine mapping `[0,1]` into `(0,∞)` (since `x u ≤ x < 1`),\nand negation flips concave to convex. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.integral_zero_one_eq_LiTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.integral_zero_one_eq_LiTwo","kind":"theorem","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogPartAConvergence.lean#L32-L44","doc":"**B3.1 — the target integral.**  `∫₀¹ −log(1 - x u)/u du = Li₂(x)` for\n`0 < x < 1`, via the change of variables `t = x u` in `LiTwo_eq_integral`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}